{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"R-2:164\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The Quran places night-and-day alternation among signs, giving وَٱلْعَصْرِ a setting within cosmic cycles.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"2:164\",\"ar\":\"وَٱخْتِلَٰفِ ٱلَّيْلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ وَٱلْفُلْكِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages name temporal movement, though 2:164 embeds it among signs of creation.\",\"limits\":\"The parallel does not identify al-ʿaṣr with a particular phase of the day-night cycle.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-2:187\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The fast is bounded by dawn and night, placing وَٱلْعَصْرِ within a measured daily interval.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"2:187\",\"ar\":\"مِنَ ٱلْفَجْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"2:187\",\"ar\":\"أَتِمُّوا۟ ٱلصِّيَامَ إِلَى ٱلَّيْلِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus can denote time, and 2:187 marks a day by its beginning and end.\",\"limits\":\"The fasting rule does not name the afternoon or connect its boundaries to this oath.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-2:196\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-2:246\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The Israelites first request combat, then most withdraw when it is prescribed; this tests resolve over a sequence and contrasts with 103:3’s counsel to patience.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"2:246\",\"ar\":\"قَالُوا۟ وَمَا لَنَآ أَلَّا نُقَٰتِلَ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ\"},{\"ref\":\"2:246\",\"ar\":\"فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ ٱلْقِتَالُ تَوَلَّوْا۟ إِلَّا قَلِيلًۭا مِّنْهُمْ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"missing\":\"A passage tying وَٱلْعَصْرِ specifically to a period of testing, or another textual link between elapsed time and steadfast action, could establish more than a thematic parallel.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-2:266\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The garden is struck by an إِعْصَارٌۭ and burns; its form shares the consonantal root of وَٱلْعَصْرِ and could add a destructive pressure image to the oath.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"2:266\",\"ar\":\"فَأَصَابَهَآ إِعْصَارٌۭ فِيهِ نَارٌۭ فَٱحْتَرَقَتْ\"}],\"missing\":\"A dictionary sense linking إِعْصَارٌۭ to the pressing sense of the focus noun, and evidence that this root echo is active in the oath, would decide whether the storm image belongs here.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-3:1\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-3:37\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-3:58\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-3:185\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The oath وَٱلْعَصْرِ precedes a claim that humanity is in loss; 3:185 gives that temporal horizon an arc from death to recompense and calls worldly life deceptive enjoyment.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:2\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لَفِى خُسْرٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"3:185\",\"ar\":\"كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ ذَآئِقَةُ ٱلْمَوْتِ\"},{\"ref\":\"3:185\",\"ar\":\"وَمَا ٱلْحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنْيَآ إِلَّا مَتَٰعُ ٱلْغُرُورِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names time and the next ayah names human loss; this parallel makes a lifetime-scale reading available.\",\"limits\":\"The parallel does not establish that al-ʿaṣr itself means an individual lifespan.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-3:190\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The closing passage of Āl ʿImrān presents night-and-day alternation as a sign for people who reflect, echoing the temporal field named by وَٱلْعَصْرِ.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"3:190\",\"ar\":\"وَٱخْتِلَٰفِ ٱلَّيْلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ لَءَايَٰتٍۢ لِّأُو۟لِى ٱلْأَلْبَٰبِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages make time perceptible through temporal movement.\",\"limits\":\"The sign in 3:190 is part of a cosmic reflection passage, with no stated relation to human loss.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-4:8\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-4:12\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-4:34\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-7:1\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-7:8\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The oath وَٱلْعَصْرِ can be heard against a scene where the decisive weighing occurs on a named day and weight determines success, sharpening the outcome implied by خُسْرٍ in 103:2.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:2\",\"ar\":\"لَفِى خُسْرٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"7:8\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْوَزْنُ يَوْمَئِذٍ ٱلْحَقُّ\"},{\"ref\":\"7:8\",\"ar\":\"فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلْمُفْلِحُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus opens a temporal oath, and 7:8 locates success at a decisive reckoning.\",\"limits\":\"The weighing scene does not identify the focus’s time with that judgment day.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-7:9\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The verb خَسِرُوا۟ shares the loss root of خُسْرٍ and makes the abstract loss in 103:2 concrete as people losing themselves through wrongdoing.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:2\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لَفِى خُسْرٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"7:9\",\"ar\":\"فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ خَسِرُوٓا۟ أَنفُسَهُم\"},{\"ref\":\"7:9\",\"ar\":\"بِمَا كَانُوا۟ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا يَظْلِمُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s loss claim is followed by an exception in 103:3; 7:9 supplies a judgment scene where loss has a stated cause.\",\"limits\":\"The shared root and outcome do not establish that the two passages describe the same event.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-7:34\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The oath by وَٱلْعَصْرِ resonates with the appointed term of each community, which cannot be advanced or delayed even an hour.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"7:34\",\"ar\":\"وَلِكُلِّ أُمَّةٍ أَجَلٌۭ\"},{\"ref\":\"7:34\",\"ar\":\"لَا يَسْتَأْخِرُونَ سَاعَةًۭ ۖ وَلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both texts make time consequential by placing limits on it.\",\"limits\":\"The term in 7:34 belongs to each community; it does not gloss the oath noun directly.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-8:37\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The label ٱلْخَٰسِرُونَ shares the loss root of خُسْرٍ, while the passage pictures the impure gathered into Hell; this gives 103:2’s human loss a sorting and outcome scene.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:2\",\"ar\":\"لَفِى خُسْرٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"8:37\",\"ar\":\"لِيَمِيزَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْخَبِيثَ مِنَ ٱلطَّيِّبِ\"},{\"ref\":\"8:37\",\"ar\":\"أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلْخَٰسِرُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s universal loss claim is qualified in 103:3; 8:37 also distinguishes groups and names the losers.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not connect its sorting to وَٱلْعَصْرِ or specify a time interval.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-10:5\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The focus’s time oath gains a measurable cosmic frame: sun and moon phases let people count years and reckon time.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"10:5\",\"ar\":\"وَقَدَّرَهُۥ مَنَازِلَ لِتَعْلَمُوا۟ عَدَدَ ٱلسِّنِينَ وَٱلْحِسَابَ\"}],\"activation\":\"Al-ʿaṣr names time, and 10:5 explicitly links celestial phases with counting and calculation.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not specify which temporal unit the oath names.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-10:24\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The transient growth and sudden cutting down in 10:24 makes وَٱلْعَصْرِ audible as time in which worldly prosperity can vanish before people expect it.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"10:24\",\"ar\":\"أَتَىٰهَآ أَمْرُنَا لَيْلًا أَوْ نَهَارًۭا فَجَعَلْنَٰهَا حَصِيدًۭا كَأَن لَّمْ تَغْنَ بِٱلْأَمْسِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus invokes time; the parable measures sudden change by night, day, and yesterday.\",\"limits\":\"The parable does not state that al-ʿaṣr is the occasion of the harvest’s destruction.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-10:49\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Asked when the promise will come, the reply invokes each community’s appointed term and says it cannot be moved by an hour; this gives وَٱلْعَصْرِ a horizon of bounded time.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"10:48\",\"ar\":\"وَيَقُولُونَ مَتَىٰ هَٰذَا ٱلْوَعْدُ\"},{\"ref\":\"10:49\",\"ar\":\"لِكُلِّ أُمَّةٍ أَجَلٌ ۚ إِذَا جَآءَ أَجَلُهُمْ فَلَا يَسْتَـْٔخِرُونَ سَاعَةًۭ ۖ وَلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The opening oath names time, and the surrounding exchange asks about the timing of a promise.\",\"limits\":\"The fixed term in 10:49 is not identified as the time sworn by in 103:1.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-10:103\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"After a call to await the days of earlier peoples, the passage names the rescue of messengers and believers; this parallels the contrast between human loss and the believing exception in Sūrat al-ʿAṣr.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:2\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لَفِى خُسْرٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟\"},{\"ref\":\"10:102\",\"ar\":\"أَيَّامِ ٱلَّذِينَ خَلَوْا۟ مِن قَبْلِهِمْ\"},{\"ref\":\"10:103\",\"ar\":\"ثُمَّ نُنَجِّى رُسُلَنَا وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s following ayat divide humanity by faith and outcome; 10:102–103 also joins a historical wait to a rescue of believers.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not make its days a definition of al-ʿaṣr.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-11:15\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The worldly interval can appear profitable: people receive their deeds’ return there and are not shortchanged, yet the next ayah reverses that apparent gain in the afterlife.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"11:15\",\"ar\":\"نُوَفِّ إِلَيْهِمْ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ فِيهَا وَهُمْ فِيهَا لَا يُبْخَسُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"11:16\",\"ar\":\"لَيْسَ لَهُمْ فِى ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ إِلَّا ٱلنَّارُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The oath names time and 103:2 declares humanity in loss; Hūd 11:15–16 distinguishes worldly return from final outcome.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not equate the focus’s time with worldly life as a specific term.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-11:16\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The voiding of deeds in the afterlife gives a concrete loss counterpart to خُسْرٍ after وَٱلْعَصْرِ: apparent work can end as no lasting gain.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:2\",\"ar\":\"لَفِى خُسْرٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"11:16\",\"ar\":\"وَحَبِطَ مَا صَنَعُوا۟ فِيهَا وَبَٰطِلٌۭ مَّا كَانُوا۟ يَعْمَلُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The surah’s oath is followed by a claim of loss, and 11:16 specifies an outcome in which deeds are nullified.\",\"limits\":\"This parallel does not specify the focus’s time as the afterlife or any particular span of life.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-11:90\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The call to seek forgiveness and turn back offers a possible redirection within the span named by وَٱلْعَصْرِ, before the passage resumes its warning.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"11:89\",\"ar\":\"أَن يُصِيبَكُم مِّثْلُ مَآ أَصَابَ قَوْمَ نُوحٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"11:90\",\"ar\":\"وَٱسْتَغْفِرُوا۟ رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوبُوٓا۟ إِلَيْهِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s next ayat distinguish loss from a faithful way forward; this passage places repentance between warning and response.\",\"limits\":\"No wording in 11:90 links repentance directly to al-ʿaṣr or to the exception in 103:3.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-12:36\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"One prisoner dreams that he presses wine, using أَعْصِرُ, a verb with the consonantal root of وَٱلْعَصْرِ; the dream could add a productive or pressing resonance to the oath.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"12:36\",\"ar\":\"إِنِّىٓ أَرَىٰنِىٓ أَعْصِرُ خَمْرًۭا\"}],\"missing\":\"A dictionary sense linking the focus noun to pressing, and evidence that this verb-to-noun root echo is active in the oath, could establish the proposed resonance.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-12:47\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Joseph’s instruction counts seven years of persistent sowing and storing, giving time an accumulated rhythm of labor and preparation beside وَٱلْعَصْرِ.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"12:47\",\"ar\":\"تَزْرَعُونَ سَبْعَ سِنِينَ دَأَبًۭا فَمَا حَصَدتُّمْ فَذَرُوهُ فِى سُنۢبُلِهِۦٓ\"}],\"activation\":\"The oath names time, and the passage measures sustained work by years.\",\"limits\":\"The agricultural instruction does not connect its year-count to the oath’s wording or meaning.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-12:49\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"After seven hard years, the promised year brings relief and people يَعْصِرُونَ; this same-root verb could let وَٱلْعَصْرِ carry a pressure-then-yield resonance.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"12:48\",\"ar\":\"سَبْعٌۭ شِدَادٌۭ يَأْكُلْنَ مَا قَدَّمْتُمْ\"},{\"ref\":\"12:49\",\"ar\":\"عَامٌۭ فِيهِ يُغَاثُ ٱلنَّاسُ وَفِيهِ يَعْصِرُونَ\"}],\"missing\":\"A dictionary account connecting the focus noun’s sense with the pressing verb, and evidence that this root relation is active across the hard-year and relief sequence, could decide the proposed reading.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-12:82\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-14:18\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The ashes of deeds scattered by wind on a stormy day picture acquired work yielding nothing, a vivid counterpart to the loss announced after وَٱلْعَصْرِ.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:2\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لَفِى خُسْرٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"14:18\",\"ar\":\"أَعْمَٰلُهُمْ كَرَمَادٍ ٱشْتَدَّتْ بِهِ ٱلرِّيحُ فِى يَوْمٍ عَاصِفٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"14:18\",\"ar\":\"لَّا يَقْدِرُونَ مِمَّا كَسَبُوا۟ عَلَىٰ شَىْءٍۢ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus links time and human loss; this parable joins a named day to the disappearance of what people earned.\",\"limits\":\"The stormy day is not identified with al-ʿaṣr, and the parallel is in outcome rather than shared wording.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-14:52\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The passage calls revelation a warning and a reminder for people of understanding, which gives a communal-message parallel to 103:3’s counsel in truth.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ\"},{\"ref\":\"14:52\",\"ar\":\"هَٰذَا بَلَٰغٌۭ لِّلنَّاسِ وَلِيُنذَرُوا۟ بِهِۦ\"},{\"ref\":\"14:52\",\"ar\":\"وَلِيَذَّكَّرَ أُو۟لُوا۟ ٱلْأَلْبَٰبِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages describe guidance meant to be received and carried among people.\",\"limits\":\"This concerns the surah’s exhortation more directly than its opening oath by time.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-16:61\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The delay of people until an appointed term, followed by an hour that cannot be advanced or postponed, gives وَٱلْعَصْرِ a frame of limited human time.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"16:61\",\"ar\":\"وَلَٰكِن يُؤَخِّرُهُمْ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٍۢ مُّسَمًّۭى\"},{\"ref\":\"16:61\",\"ar\":\"فَإِذَا جَآءَ أَجَلُهُمْ لَا يَسْتَـْٔخِرُونَ سَاعَةًۭ ۖ وَلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus invokes time, while this passage describes a deferred but fixed endpoint.\",\"limits\":\"The appointed term here is not expressly named by al-ʿaṣr.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-16:118\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"X1\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Across these passages, each community’s أَجَلٌ ends on time, with no advance or delay even by an hour; this repeated formula gives وَٱلْعَصْرِ a Quranic backdrop of bounded, appointed time.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"7:34\",\"ar\":\"لَا يَسْتَأْخِرُونَ سَاعَةًۭ ۖ وَلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"10:49\",\"ar\":\"فَلَا يَسْتَـْٔخِرُونَ سَاعَةًۭ ۖ وَلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"16:61\",\"ar\":\"لَا يَسْتَـْٔخِرُونَ سَاعَةًۭ ۖ وَلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The oath opens Sūrat al-ʿAṣr by naming time; three passages elsewhere articulate its fixed endpoints with a recurring formula.\",\"limits\":\"The repeated formula concerns appointed communal or human terms and does not lexically define al-ʿaṣr.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
